# Toggleable waybar modules, read by modules.sh (see PIN.md).
# Format:  key|label|module-id [module-id...]
#   key       what you type / the leader-menu leaf
#   label     shown in `modules.sh list` and the picker
#   module-id one or more waybar module ids, toggled as a group
#
# Only custom modules can be listed here: the toggle works by making a module's
# exec print nothing, which built-in modules (cpu, clock, tray...) cannot do.
# Adding a row is not enough - the module's exec must also be wrapped in
# `modules.sh gate <id>` and given a "signal" in config.base / config.pin-full (10, unless it owns one).

needs|Needs you: what only you can do|custom/needs
agents|Agent sessions by world|custom/ai-agents
health|System health|custom/health
projects|Projects: progress per project|custom/projects
queue|Queue: whether agent work flows, and what to fix|custom/queue
fleet|Fleet health|custom/fleet
load|CPU and load (fleet on hover)|custom/load
ci|CI runners|custom/ci
printer|3D printers|custom/printer
caffeine|Caffeine: keep this machine awake|custom/caffeine
mode|Machine mode|custom/machine-mode
timebox|Timebox|custom/timebox
storage|Disk usage|custom/storage
machines|Machines (pin only)|custom/machines

# Not listed: the custom/act-* pin buttons. They are static icons with no exec, and
# the toggle works by gating an exec, so there is nothing to hide without spawning a
# process per button per interval.
